<wpt lat="50.579000" lon="7.242500"><name>Ludendorff Bridge, Remagen — Peace Museum (Germany &amp; Austria)</name><desc>Tour day 1

The railway bridge captured intact on 7 March that put the first Americans across the Rhine; it collapsed ten days later. The surviving towers hold the Peace Museum.

Stand at the tower and look at the river's width — this was the wall the Allies expected to fight for.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/germany-austria.html

DZ Charlie field guides · dzcharlie.com</desc><link href="https://dzcharlie.com/germany-austria.html"><text>Open the guide</text></link><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Germany &amp; Austria · Tour stops</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="51.122800" lon="6.844300"><name>Zons — the walled town on the Rhine (Germany &amp; Austria)</name><desc>Tour day 1

A medieval customs town on the 506th's stretch of river, untouched by the war, between Cologne and Dormagen. The dike path north of it is the regiment's April 1945 outpost line.

Walk the dike north toward Stürzelberg.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/germany-austria.html

