<wpt lat="47.590000" lon="12.987000"><name>Königssee (Germany &amp; Austria)</name><desc>Tour day 4

The fjord-like lake below the Watzmann, where the 506th swam and boated in May 1945. Electric boats to St Bartholomä; the echo trumpet still plays.

A rest from the museums.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/germany-austria.html

DZ Charlie field guides · dzcharlie.com</desc><link href="https://dzcharlie.com/germany-austria.html"><text>Open the guide</text></link><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Germany &amp; Austria · Tour stops</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.324050" lon="12.801200"><name>Grand Hotel Zell am See — regimental HQ (Germany &amp; Austria)</name><desc>Tour day 5

Sink's headquarters on the promontory in the lake; the ballroom and terrace are as the regiment knew them. Still a hotel — coffee on the terrace is allowed.

Look across to Thumersbach: the whole valley was the regiment's.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/germany-austria.html

DZ Charlie field guides · dzcharlie.com</desc><link href="https://dzcharlie.com/germany-austria.html"><text>Open the guide</text></link><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Germany &amp; Austria · Tour stops</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.162500" lon="12.717500"><name>Kaprun high-mountain dams (Mooserboden) (Germany &amp; Austria)</name><desc>Tour day 5

The hydro-electric project begun in 1938 with forced and slave labour from the camps; the 506th guarded the site and its DP camp in 1945. Finished after the war as a symbol of Austrian reconstruction. Bus and inclined lift to the dams; exhibition &quot;Erlebniswelt Strom&quot;.

Read the memorial to the forced labourers at the dam.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/germany-austria.html

